
| Control Statement / Concept          | Syntax / Example                                                                  | Explanation                                                                                               |
| ------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Control Statements**               | `if`, `for`, `while`, etc.                                                        | Control statements control the **flow/order in which Python code executes**.                              |
| **Main Types**                       | Decision, Loop, Jump                                                              | Python control flow can be understood as **decision-making, repetition, and changing the normal flow**.   |
| **`if` Statement**                   | `if age >= 18:`                                                                   | Executes a block only when the condition is `True`.                                                       |
| **`if` Example**                     | `if x > 10:`<br>    `print("Big")`                                                | If `x > 10` is true, `"Big"` is printed.                                                                  |
| **Condition**                        | `x > 10`                                                                          | A condition produces either `True` or `False`.                                                            |
| **Boolean Values**                   | `True`, `False`                                                                   | Python uses Boolean values to make decisions.                                                             |
| **`else` Statement**                 | `if x > 10:`<br>    `...`<br>`else:`<br>    `...`                                 | `else` runs when the `if` condition is `False`.                                                           |
| **`if-else`**                        | `if age >= 18:`<br>    `print("Adult")`<br>`else:`<br>    `print("Minor")`        | Chooses between two possible blocks.                                                                      |
| **`elif`**                           | `if x > 0:`<br>`elif x < 0:`                                                      | `elif` means **else if**. It checks another condition when the previous condition is false.               |
| **Multiple `elif`**                  | `if marks >= 90:`<br>`elif marks >= 80:`<br>`elif marks >= 70:`                   | You can have multiple `elif` conditions.                                                                  |
| **`if-elif-else`**                   | `if condition:`<br>`elif condition:`<br>`else:`                                   | Used when there are multiple possible conditions/results.                                                 |
| **Nested `if`**                      | `if age >= 18:`<br>    `if citizen:`                                              | An `if` statement inside another `if` statement.                                                          |
| **Nested `if-else`**                 | `if x > 0:`<br>    `if x % 2 == 0:`                                               | Useful when one decision depends on another decision.                                                     |
| **One-line `if`**                    | `if x > 10: print(x)`                                                             | A simple `if` can be written on one line.                                                                 |
| **Ternary / Conditional Expression** | `msg = "Adult" if age >= 18 else "Minor"`                                         | A short one-line form of `if-else`.                                                                       |
| **Comparison Operators**             | `>`, `<`, `>=`, `<=`, `==`, `!=`                                                  | Used to compare values and create conditions.                                                             |
| **`==`**                             | `x == 10`                                                                         | Checks whether two values are equal.                                                                      |
| **`!=`**                             | `x != 10`                                                                         | Checks whether two values are not equal.                                                                  |
| **`>`**                              | `x > 10`                                                                          | Checks whether `x` is greater than `10`.                                                                  |
| **`<`**                              | `x < 10`                                                                          | Checks whether `x` is less than `10`.                                                                     |
| **`>=`**                             | `x >= 10`                                                                         | Checks whether `x` is greater than or equal to `10`.                                                      |
| **`<=`**                             | `x <= 10`                                                                         | Checks whether `x` is less than or equal to `10`.                                                         |
| **Logical `and`**                    | `age >= 18 and age <= 60`                                                         | Both conditions must be `True`.                                                                           |
| **Logical `or`**                     | `x == 5 or x == 10`                                                               | At least one condition must be `True`.                                                                    |
| **Logical `not`**                    | `not is_valid`                                                                    | Reverses a Boolean value.                                                                                 |
| **Membership `in`**                  | `"a" in "apple"`                                                                  | Checks whether a value exists inside a sequence.                                                          |
| **Membership `not in`**              | `"z" not in "apple"`                                                              | Checks whether a value does not exist in a sequence.                                                      |
| **`for` Loop**                       | `for i in range(5):`                                                              | Repeats code for each item in a sequence/iterable.                                                        |
| **`range()`**                        | `range(5)`                                                                        | Produces numbers `0` through `4`.                                                                         |
| **`range(start, stop)`**             | `range(1, 6)`                                                                     | Produces `1, 2, 3, 4, 5`. The stop value is excluded.                                                     |
| **`range(start, stop, step)`**       | `range(1, 10, 2)`                                                                 | Starts at `1`, stops before `10`, and increases by `2`.                                                   |
| **Loop through String**              | `for ch in "Python":`                                                             | Processes each character one by one.                                                                      |
| **Loop through List**                | `for x in [10, 20, 30]:`                                                          | Processes each list element.                                                                              |
| **Loop through Tuple**               | `for x in (1, 2, 3):`                                                             | Processes each tuple element.                                                                             |
| **Loop through Dictionary**          | `for key in data:`                                                                | By default, loops through dictionary keys.                                                                |
| **`while` Loop**                     | `while x < 5:`                                                                    | Repeats code as long as the condition remains `True`.                                                     |
| **`while` Example**                  | `x = 1`<br>`while x <= 5:`<br>    `print(x)`<br>    `x += 1`                      | Prints numbers from `1` to `5`.                                                                           |
| **Infinite Loop**                    | `while True:`                                                                     | Creates a loop that continues forever unless stopped with `break` or another control mechanism.           |
| **`break`**                          | `if x == 5:`<br>    `break`                                                       | Immediately stops the current loop.                                                                       |
| **`continue`**                       | `if x == 5:`<br>    `continue`                                                    | Skips the current iteration and moves to the next iteration.                                              |
| **`pass`**                           | `if x > 5:`<br>    `pass`                                                         | Does nothing. Used as a placeholder when code is required syntactically but you don't want an action yet. |
| **`break` vs `continue`**            | `break` / `continue`                                                              | `break` **ends the loop**; `continue` **skips one iteration**.                                            |
| **Nested Loop**                      | `for i in range(3):`<br>    `for j in range(3):`                                  | A loop inside another loop.                                                                               |
| **`for-else`**                       | `for x in nums:`<br>    `...`<br>`else:`<br>    `...`                             | The `else` runs when the loop finishes normally, without `break`.                                         |
| **`while-else`**                     | `while condition:`<br>    `...`<br>`else:`<br>    `...`                           | The `else` runs when the `while` loop ends normally.                                                      |
| **`break` with loop-else**           | `for x in nums:`<br>    `if x == 5: break`<br>`else:`<br>    `print("Not found")` | Useful for searching: `else` executes only if `break` never happens.                                      |
| **Exception Control**                | `try`, `except`, `else`, `finally`                                                | Controls what happens when an error/exception occurs.                                                     |
| **`try`**                            | `try:`<br>    `x = 10 / 0`                                                        | Contains code that might produce an exception.                                                            |
| **`except`**                         | `except ZeroDivisionError:`                                                       | Handles a specific exception.                                                                             |
| **`else` with `try`**                | `try:`<br>    `...`<br>`except:`<br>    `...`<br>`else:`<br>    `...`             | `else` runs when the `try` block completes without an exception.                                          |
| **`finally`**                        | `finally:`<br>    `print("Done")`                                                 | Runs whether an exception occurs or not.                                                                  |
| **`raise`**                          | `raise ValueError("Invalid")`                                                     | Manually raises an exception.                                                                             |
| **`return`**                         | `return result`                                                                   | Exits a function and optionally sends a value back.                                                       |
| **`return` inside loop**             | `def test():`<br>    `for x in nums:`<br>        `return x`                       | `return` exits the entire function, not just the loop.                                                    |
| **Indentation**                      | `if x > 5:`<br>    `print(x)`                                                     | Python uses indentation to define code blocks.                                                            |
| **Block**                            | `if`, `for`, `while`, `def`                                                       | A block is a group of statements controlled by a statement such as `if` or `for`.                         |
| **Short-circuit `and`**              | `False and something`                                                             | Python may stop evaluating as soon as the result is known to be `False`.                                  |
| **Short-circuit `or`**               | `True or something`                                                               | Python may stop evaluating as soon as the result is known to be `True`.                                   |
| **Decision Making**                  | `if / elif / else`                                                                | Used when the program needs to choose what to do.                                                         |
| **Repetition**                       | `for / while`                                                                     | Used when the program needs to repeat code.                                                               |
| **Jump / Flow Change**               | `break / continue / pass / return`                                                | Changes or controls the normal execution flow.                                                            |
| **Exception Flow**                   | `try / except / finally`                                                          | Controls program execution when errors occur.                                                             |
